diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index 841a734..a0d71c4 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -310,6 +310,14 @@ and its latest line is the review-complete feature prompt. `TerminalUi` queues o
 a chat transitions into that ready state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain
 highlighted until the user answers or sends a follow-up.
 
+Command mode supports Vim-style visual selection in whichever pane has focus. `v` starts character
+selection, `V` starts line selection, and `Ctrl-V` starts block selection. `h`, `j`, `k`, `l`, and
+the arrow keys extend the active selection without entering chat-edit movement, `y` yanks the active
+selection, and `Y` yanks linewise text. Yanks are emitted as OSC52 clipboard sequences in the next
+render frame and reported through the status line. `TerminalApp` and `UiHarness` refresh
+`TerminalUi` with the currently rendered right-pane text and chat cursor column before routing
+visual keys, so right-pane selections use the same visible text that the user is selecting.
+
 `src/ui.rs::TerminalUi` owns terminal-specific presentation state:
 
 - `UiMode`, `PaneFocus`, `UiSurface`, `UiKey`, and `UiAction` model terminal interactions.
